# SPSSiteLifecycle line-ending and encoding policy
#
# PowerShell files are stored with a UTF-8 BOM (the BOM is part of the committed content)
# and checked out with CRLF, like the other SPS* repositories. The BOM keeps non-ASCII
# characters readable by every host, and CRLF is native on the Windows machines the tool
# runs on.
#
# YAML, Markdown and other text files must NOT carry a BOM (it breaks some YAML
# parsers and is unwanted on GitHub-rendered files); they use LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell -- committed with a UTF-8 BOM, checked out with CRLF
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.psm1  text eol=crlf
*.psd1  text eol=crlf

# Workflows / docs / config -- no BOM, LF
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# CSV fixtures are stored byte for byte, so that a file saved by Excel (BOM, CRLF line
# endings, semicolons) is tested exactly as written
*.csv   -text

# Binary-ish artifacts
*.png binary
*.zip binary
